-shareholdings, parent-company holdings, and insider holdings). For point-in-time fiscal-year analysis, keep using sharesIssued in each annual row. Confirmed values are cross-checked against quarterly earnings PDFs published on each company's IR site for data quality assurance (canonical source: each company's IR PDF). IMPORTANT — splitAdjustmentFactor lag: this snapshot reflects post-FYE stock splits immediately (next-day after quarterly disclosure), but the per-row split_adjustment_factor in 'data' above is sourced from split_events (5-layer detection: yuho text-block regex, sharesIssued YoY inference, decision-disclosure capture, prior_inferred from XBRL Current/Prior ratio, and manual override). For post-FYE splits, split_adjustment_factor typically updates within 1–2 business days of the decision-disclosure capture, or upon next annual filing — until then the latest annual row may show split_adjustment_factor = 1.0 while the snapshot already reflects the post-split share count. To detect this transient state client-side, compare snapshot.shares_outstanding / data[-1].sharesIssued: if the ratio is an integer near 2/3/4/5/10 (±2%) and data[-1].split_adjustment_factor = 1.0, treat the row as in-flight and rely on snapshot.shares_outstanding for market-cap. We monitor this invariant daily with an internal alert. Please report any persistent mismatch (>5 business days) to feedback@edinetdb.jp. See docs/field-notes/latest_shares_snapshot.md.","quarter":1,"shares_outstanding":17699367,"shares_outstanding_excluding_treasury":16984130,"source":"latest_quarterly_earnings_disclosure","treasury_shares":715237},"non_consolidated_fields":["avg_annual_salary","dividend_per_share","payout_ratio_reported","revenue_non_consolidated","shares_issued"],"period":"annual"}}